WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:32.599
[Action introductory
music playing]

00:00:32.599 --> 00:00:38.571
[Suspenseful music plays]

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:40.840
Cadmium: I am really
sorry, this doesn't

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:42.809
fit our model here at S.H.H.

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:45.578
Cadmium: I mean, armed
security MUSHROOMS?!

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:46.346
Cadmium: Really?!

00:00:46.346 --> 00:00:48.148
How do you expect
that to work?

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:52.018
[Waiting room
music playing]

00:00:52.018 --> 00:00:54.120
Fun Guy Fern: Commander
Cadmium, you won't regret this!

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.822
I mean, look at
this mushroom!

00:00:55.822 --> 00:00:57.724
Fun Guy Fern: It has
a little cop hat on!

00:00:57.724 --> 00:01:00.326
I mean-[nervous
laughter]-I'm intimidated!

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:03.897
C: Look-Fun Guy Fern-you got
your start here at S.H.H., and

00:01:03.897 --> 00:01:06.966
I respect you, but
my answer is "no".

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:09.035
[Notification sounds]

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:14.340
C: Ah, Agents Aeon and
Amethyst, come in!

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:16.376
Fern was... just leaving.

00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:19.979
C: Sit down you two.

00:01:22.482 --> 00:01:23.650
Aeon: What is
it, Commander?

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:25.418
C: Starting early
today, I'm afraid.

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:27.921
C: We have reports that
the Hawthorne Hipster is on

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:31.758
the outskirts of town making
some kind of huge bonfire.

00:01:31.758 --> 00:01:33.726
C: It's raising quite
the ruckus out there.

00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:34.828
Get on it you two!

00:01:34.828 --> 00:01:36.496
Amethyst: Sure
thing, Commander.

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:40.066
Amethyst: I don't get it.

00:01:40.066 --> 00:01:42.702
Why's the Commander so
upset about a bonfire?

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:44.270
Amethyst: I
mean-sure-it's annoying,

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:45.972
but why get us involved?

00:01:45.972 --> 00:01:47.006
Aeon: Don't you get it?

00:01:47.006 --> 00:01:48.942
Cadmium's worried about
all the particulate matter

00:01:48.942 --> 00:01:50.844
being given off
by the bonfire.

00:01:50.844 --> 00:01:52.679
Aeon: You know,
particulate matter?

00:01:52.679 --> 00:01:54.714
It's a mixture of tiny
solid particles and

00:01:54.714 --> 00:01:57.016
liquid droplets found
in the atmosphere.

00:01:57.016 --> 00:02:00.019
Amethyst: It can also be known
as "particle pollution."

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:02.856
Amethyst: So little particles
get in the air, so what?

00:02:02.856 --> 00:02:05.892
Aeon: Well, sometimes the
particles are just soil or dust,

00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:07.961
but other times
organic chemicals, and

00:02:07.961 --> 00:02:09.662
metals can become airborne.

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:12.232
Amethyst: Consider
this-the Hawthorne Hipster is

00:02:12.232 --> 00:02:14.100
burning SOMETHING out there.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:16.669
Amethyst: When she lights
the fire, smoke is given off.

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:18.738
Amethyst: That smoke will
contain tiny particles of

00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:20.874
whatever chemicals
were in her fire.

00:02:20.874 --> 00:02:22.041
Amethyst: [suspenseful
music] So if the chemical is

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:23.943
highly toxic...

00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:25.712
Aeon:...Then it's
getting into the air.

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:26.813
Amethyst: Then we
better get on it!

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:28.081
Let's go!

00:02:28.081 --> 00:02:30.750
[action music]

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:33.553
Amethyst: So how do all these
particles get in the air anyway?

00:02:33.553 --> 00:02:36.990
Aeon: Well, human activities
like construction, mining,

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:38.691
processing metals or stones, or

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:41.027
combustion can
release particles.

00:02:41.027 --> 00:02:44.797
Amethyst: Eh-combustion,
like bonfires...or burning

00:02:44.797 --> 00:02:47.767
fuel to make
your car run-no?

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:50.169
Aeon: Yes-burning fossil
fuels will release

00:02:50.169 --> 00:02:51.604
particles in the air.

00:02:51.604 --> 00:02:53.439
Aeon: That's why the
agency gives us these cars

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:54.874
that run on kale.

00:02:54.874 --> 00:02:56.910
It's not just human
activity though.

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:59.712
Aeon: Pollen, sea salt,
or dust can be blown around

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:01.147
from just the wind.

00:03:01.147 --> 00:03:03.850
Aeon: Or wildfires and
volcanic activity can release

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:07.020
massive amounts of
particles in the air naturally.

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:08.888
Amethyst: [gasp]
Volcanic activity!

00:03:08.888 --> 00:03:12.292
Like that time with the giant
chicken-in the theme song!

00:03:12.292 --> 00:03:14.561
Aeon: Yeah, they never
show the coolest parts

00:03:14.561 --> 00:03:15.828
from the theme song...

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:18.631
[action music]

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:22.001
Hipster: Over-produced,
big record label garbage!

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:22.769
Amethyst: Hey!

00:03:22.769 --> 00:03:24.137
Hawthorn Hipster!

00:03:24.137 --> 00:03:25.672
Knock it off!

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:30.510
Aeon: By the authority
given to us by S.H.H.

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:32.912
we order you to
cease and desist.

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:36.149
Aeon: You are being a MAJOR
source of pollution right now.

00:03:36.149 --> 00:03:37.016
H: Really?

00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:40.486
How is this any worse than
the noise pollution caused by

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:44.157
Tailyn Rift and her
poppy, mainstream sound?

00:03:44.157 --> 00:03:46.526
H: You should
be thanking me.

00:03:46.526 --> 00:03:48.027
Amethyst: Well, actually,
we're more concerned with all

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:50.897
the particulate matter
you're releasing into the air.

00:03:50.897 --> 00:03:52.832
Amethyst: Those albums are
covered in plastic, and

00:03:52.832 --> 00:03:55.401
all the chemicals in them
and the wood are thrown into

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:57.170
the air through that smoke.

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:58.004
H: So?

00:03:58.004 --> 00:04:01.741
I'm sending Tailyn Rift's
terrible music into the sky

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:04.177
where it can't
hurt anyone anymore.

00:04:04.177 --> 00:04:06.245
Aeon: See, that's where
you're wrong, Hipster.

00:04:06.245 --> 00:04:08.748
Aeon: All those chemicals
going into the air could make

00:04:08.748 --> 00:04:11.918
people way more ill than
country/pop fusion music.

00:04:11.918 --> 00:04:13.653
Aeon: Depending on the
kind of particulate matter and

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:16.356
the level of exposure,
people who breathe in this

00:04:16.356 --> 00:04:19.659
smoke could have exaggerated
respiratory symptoms, like

00:04:19.659 --> 00:04:22.061
coughing or difficult breathing,

00:04:22.061 --> 00:04:24.731
Aeon: aggravated asthma,
decreased lung functions,

00:04:24.731 --> 00:04:27.867
irregular heartbeat,
nonfatal heart attacks, or

00:04:27.867 --> 00:04:31.237
premature death if that person
has heart or lung disease.

00:04:31.237 --> 00:04:34.607
H: Clearly, you've never
heard these songs...

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:36.409
Amethyst: And this fire
is particularly bad

00:04:36.409 --> 00:04:37.977
because of the plastic.

00:04:37.977 --> 00:04:40.913
Amethyst: Some particles
are called primary particles.

00:04:40.913 --> 00:04:43.549
This matter is directly
released from the source.

00:04:43.549 --> 00:04:45.485
Amethyst: This could
include dust or ash that's

00:04:45.485 --> 00:04:47.020
coming from this fire.

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:48.821
Aeon: What we're more
concerned with right now are

00:04:48.821 --> 00:04:51.024
the secondary particles
from your fire.

00:04:51.024 --> 00:04:53.459
Aeon: Those chemicals in
the plastic are forming

00:04:53.459 --> 00:04:55.028
secondary particles.

00:04:55.028 --> 00:04:56.829
Aeon: These are particles
that form from chemical

00:04:56.829 --> 00:04:58.698
reactions in
the atmosphere.

00:04:58.698 --> 00:05:01.067
Aeon: Secondary particles
are the majority of

00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:03.970
particulate matter in
the US and are commonly

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:06.706
released by power plants
and automobiles, and

00:05:06.706 --> 00:05:09.042
YOU, Hawthorn Hipster.

00:05:09.042 --> 00:05:11.878
H: You still don't
get it, do you?!

00:05:11.878 --> 00:05:15.014
H: I am burdened with
a glorious purpose!

00:05:15.014 --> 00:05:18.451
I am freeing us from
corporate trends!

00:05:18.451 --> 00:05:20.553
Amethyst: Eh-she's
not getting it.

00:05:20.553 --> 00:05:22.288
Aeon: Nope, we're going to
need one of those

00:05:22.288 --> 00:05:25.591
blank backgrounds for
educational things to happen on.

00:05:25.591 --> 00:05:26.359
Amethyst: Oh, goody!

00:05:26.359 --> 00:05:27.994
I love those!

00:05:27.994 --> 00:05:29.562
Yep, fly it in.

00:05:29.562 --> 00:05:32.432
H: This place reminds
me of my soul.

00:05:32.432 --> 00:05:35.334
Amethyst: Wait-are
you hipster or emo?

00:05:35.334 --> 00:05:37.470
You've got to keep your
writing consistent.

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:39.305
Aeon: Ok you two, look.

00:05:39.305 --> 00:05:41.641
This is a human hair.

00:05:41.641 --> 00:05:43.843
Aeon: To us, they seem
very thin, but by

00:05:43.843 --> 00:05:46.412
particulate matter
scale, it's pretty big.

00:05:46.412 --> 00:05:50.450
Aeon: One human hair is about
50-70 micrometers in diameter.

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:52.919
Aeon: Here's a little
piece of particulate matter.

00:05:52.919 --> 00:05:55.421
This could represent
dust or pollen.

00:05:55.421 --> 00:05:58.091
Aeon: It's about 10
micrometers in diameter.

00:05:58.091 --> 00:05:59.225
That's pretty tiny.

00:05:59.225 --> 00:06:00.593
H: Dusty Pollen?

00:06:00.593 --> 00:06:03.696
They sold out after
their first album.

00:06:03.696 --> 00:06:06.833
Aeon: You're going to have a
very rich career as a barista.

00:06:06.833 --> 00:06:08.301
Amethyst: So if that
particle is only about

00:06:08.301 --> 00:06:11.237
10 micrometers in diameter,
that means we could stretch

00:06:11.237 --> 00:06:13.740
five of them across
one human hair.

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:16.909
Aeon: Exactly, now check
this particle out.

00:06:16.909 --> 00:06:19.946
H: Yeah, I can't
see that at all.

00:06:19.946 --> 00:06:21.514
Aeon: It is pretty
hard to see.

00:06:21.514 --> 00:06:24.283
Aeon: This kind of particulate
matter represents metals,

00:06:24.283 --> 00:06:27.754
organic compounds, or particles formed from combustion.

00:06:27.754 --> 00:06:30.890
Aeon: Like the chemicals coming
out of your burning plastic.

00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:33.192
Amethyst: So how many
micrometers is that one?

00:06:33.192 --> 00:06:36.896
Aeon: This is only 2.5
micrometers in diameter.

00:06:36.896 --> 00:06:39.465
Aeon: That's so small that
four of them could fit across

00:06:39.465 --> 00:06:42.902
the diameter of one of
our 10 micrometer particles.

00:06:42.902 --> 00:06:46.172
H: Well, if these
particles are so tiny,

00:06:46.172 --> 00:06:48.441
why would they cause
health problems?

00:06:48.441 --> 00:06:51.410
H: Shouldn't they just slip
right through our bodies?

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:53.846
Aeon: You might think that,
but the particles ranging from

00:06:53.846 --> 00:06:57.083
2.5 to 10 micrometers
are the most dangerous

00:06:57.083 --> 00:06:59.118
types of particle pollution.

00:06:59.118 --> 00:07:02.822
Aeon: In fact, particles that
are 2.5 to 10 micrometers in

00:07:02.822 --> 00:07:06.425
diameter are what particulate
pollution is defined as.

00:07:06.425 --> 00:07:08.494
Amethyst: I would guess that's
because the 10 micrometer

00:07:08.494 --> 00:07:11.097
particles-like pollen-are
small enough to get in

00:07:11.097 --> 00:07:13.599
your lungs and
aggravate allergies.

00:07:13.599 --> 00:07:15.601
Aeon: Yep, and the
smallest particles are

00:07:15.601 --> 00:07:17.904
the most dangerous, because
they're small enough to

00:07:17.904 --> 00:07:19.639
get into your blood vessels.

00:07:19.639 --> 00:07:22.041
Aeon: That's when some
major concerns can happen.

00:07:22.041 --> 00:07:24.977
H: Hey, why's it
foggy in here?

00:07:24.977 --> 00:07:27.613
H: Fog is SO mainstream!

00:07:27.613 --> 00:07:31.350
Amethyst: [Sighs] So-particulate
pollution is not just a health

00:07:31.350 --> 00:07:35.988
concern; it also contributes
to reduced visibility and haze.

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:39.025
H: What's that thing?

00:07:39.025 --> 00:07:41.127
Aeon: That's a carbon
monoxide molecule.

00:07:41.127 --> 00:07:43.462
Aeon: It's an incredibly
tiny little molecule that

00:07:43.462 --> 00:07:45.331
can cause big problems.

00:07:45.331 --> 00:07:48.634
Amethyst: When you burn
plastics, fossil fuels, wood,

00:07:48.634 --> 00:07:52.772
run a car, or smoke tobacco,
you produce carbon monoxide.

00:07:52.772 --> 00:07:57.276
H: Well it sounds like it's
already everywhere, sell out!

00:07:57.276 --> 00:07:58.177
Aeon: It is!

00:07:58.177 --> 00:08:01.681
Carbon monoxide is most
commonly found in car exhausts,

00:08:01.681 --> 00:08:04.483
but it can also be found
in homes with gas furnaces,

00:08:04.483 --> 00:08:07.153
chimneys, or
malfunctioning appliances.

00:08:07.153 --> 00:08:08.321
Amethyst: The bigger
problem is what

00:08:08.321 --> 00:08:10.723
carbon monoxide
does in your body.

00:08:10.723 --> 00:08:13.226
Amethyst: Since carbon
monoxide is so small,

00:08:13.226 --> 00:08:14.927
it can get in your blood.

00:08:14.927 --> 00:08:17.129
Amethyst: Carbon monoxide
happens to attach well

00:08:17.129 --> 00:08:18.731
to your red blood cells.

00:08:18.731 --> 00:08:20.600
Amethyst: This converts
that chemical that carries

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:24.070
oxygen in your blood,
hemoglobin, and converts it into

00:08:24.070 --> 00:08:26.973
a chemical called
carboxyhemoglobin.

00:08:26.973 --> 00:08:28.875
H: I was listening to
hemoglobin back when

00:08:28.875 --> 00:08:30.543
it was just globin.

00:08:30.543 --> 00:08:33.579
Amethyst: You-you-HAVE to be
making this stuff up, right?

00:08:33.579 --> 00:08:36.182
Aero: Without hemoglobin
to carry oxygen to your body,

00:08:36.182 --> 00:08:38.784
you may experience
headaches, dizziness,

00:08:38.784 --> 00:08:41.787
fatigue, chest pain,
difficulty breathing,

00:08:41.787 --> 00:08:45.191
memory loss, or flu-like
symptoms in the short term.

00:08:45.191 --> 00:08:47.727
Aero: However, if you are
exposed to too much of it,

00:08:47.727 --> 00:08:50.062
you could develop heart
disease, damage your

00:08:50.062 --> 00:08:53.699
nervous system, go into
a coma, or even die!

00:08:53.699 --> 00:08:57.737
H: ...Ok, I have to admit,
that's kind of scary.

00:08:57.737 --> 00:08:59.538
H: I'll make sure my
fire doesn't release

00:08:59.538 --> 00:09:01.440
any carbon monoxide.

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:04.043
Amethyst: That's the thing,
since carbon monoxide is

00:09:04.043 --> 00:09:06.412
colorless and
odorless-you won't

00:09:06.412 --> 00:09:08.547
even notice it's around.

00:09:08.547 --> 00:09:09.649
H: [alarmed] W-What?!

00:09:09.649 --> 00:09:11.851
B-b-but how can I avoid it?!

00:09:11.851 --> 00:09:13.486
Amethyst: Well, to start-[car
engine sound]-make sure to

00:09:13.486 --> 00:09:17.323
never leave your car running in your garage with the door shut.

00:09:17.323 --> 00:09:19.025
Amethyst: The carbon
monoxide could build up.

00:09:19.025 --> 00:09:21.961
Aero: Also, make sure to get
your exhaust system regularly

00:09:21.961 --> 00:09:24.730
checked to prevent
carbon monoxide leaks.

00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:26.632
Mechanic: Hey, so your
suspension looks to have

00:09:26.632 --> 00:09:29.302
leaked brake fluid all over
the internal drive shaft

00:09:29.302 --> 00:09:32.638
which has just completely
corroded the flux capacitor.

00:09:32.638 --> 00:09:35.708
Mechanic: That's going to
run you about $35,000.

00:09:35.708 --> 00:09:38.811
Amethyst: Well, that sounds
like an honest assessment.

00:09:38.811 --> 00:09:40.212
Is this enough?!

00:09:40.212 --> 00:09:42.682
Aero: Securing your
house is important too.

00:09:42.682 --> 00:09:44.550
Aero: Never use portable
flameless heaters in the

00:09:44.550 --> 00:09:47.954
house or burn anything in
an area that isn't vented.

00:09:47.954 --> 00:09:50.523
Aero: You can also install
a carbon monoxide detector in

00:09:50.523 --> 00:09:53.192
your house to warn
you of unsafe levels.

00:09:53.192 --> 00:09:56.128
Aero: Remember, it's just
like a smoke alarm and needs to

00:09:56.128 --> 00:09:58.597
have its batteries
replaced regularly.

00:09:58.597 --> 00:10:00.399
Amethyst: You could also
make sure your fireplace is

00:10:00.399 --> 00:10:02.635
well-vented and clean.

00:10:02.635 --> 00:10:03.703
Chimney sweep:
Evening guv'nah.

00:10:03.703 --> 00:10:05.638
Chimney sweep: You haven't
seen a practically perfect lady

00:10:05.638 --> 00:10:07.373
come through here, have you?

00:10:07.373 --> 00:10:09.375
Amethyst: Not without
violating a copyright!

00:10:09.375 --> 00:10:10.376
CS: Cheers!

00:10:10.376 --> 00:10:13.612
[music plays]

00:10:13.612 --> 00:10:15.614
Aero: It' not just
carbon monoxide, either.

00:10:15.614 --> 00:10:19.085
Aero: Burnings can also
release nitrogen oxides.

00:10:19.085 --> 00:10:21.654
Aero: These chemicals can
come in contact with rain and

00:10:21.654 --> 00:10:22.955
become acid rain.

00:10:22.955 --> 00:10:24.857
Aero: Acid rain can change
the chemistry of our

00:10:24.857 --> 00:10:27.059
environment and
affect our health.

00:10:27.059 --> 00:10:30.062
Amethyst: Or you could be
releasing sulfur dioxide.

00:10:30.062 --> 00:10:31.998
Amethyst: It smells
AWFUL, and it makes you

00:10:31.998 --> 00:10:33.699
feel like you're suffocating.

00:10:33.699 --> 00:10:35.568
Amethyst: Not only is it
gross, it can burn your

00:10:35.568 --> 00:10:39.438
skin and eyes or cause
respiratory irritation.

00:10:39.438 --> 00:10:40.906
Aero: And who knows
what other effects

00:10:40.906 --> 00:10:42.908
the chemicals you're
releasing could have?!

00:10:45.511 --> 00:10:46.312
Cop: All right!

00:10:46.312 --> 00:10:48.614
Time to put this fire out!

00:10:48.614 --> 00:10:49.915
-[sniff sniff]-

00:10:49.915 --> 00:10:53.386
woah-what's in the air
here-I suddenly feel like-

00:10:53.386 --> 00:10:55.021
Cop: [starts singing]
-Oh-I'm fifteen!

00:10:55.021 --> 00:10:57.757
-and it's really hard-and
dad's on a tractor-and

00:10:57.757 --> 00:10:59.425
the boy doesn't like me-

00:10:59.425 --> 00:11:01.360
Cop: -why won't he go
to the dance with me!?

00:11:01.360 --> 00:11:02.628
-I'm fifteen!

00:11:02.628 --> 00:11:04.463
-uh-fifteen's-uh-tough!

00:11:04.463 --> 00:11:05.898
Hipster: Aaah! OK!

00:11:05.898 --> 00:11:06.632
I'll put it out!

00:11:06.632 --> 00:11:08.367
I'll put it out!

00:11:13.072 --> 00:11:15.007
Amethyst: I'm glad we
could solve this situation

00:11:15.007 --> 00:11:17.710
without tempers [brief
pause]-flaring-

00:11:17.710 --> 00:11:20.513
Aero: [unimpressed sigh] I
don't get paid enough for this.

00:11:20.513 --> 00:11:21.914
Amethyst: Hey! Come on!

00:11:21.914 --> 00:11:24.183
We need to work on
our-witty agent banter!

00:11:28.821 --> 00:11:31.090
Amethyst: Oh gosh-hey, we need
to make a quick stop before

00:11:31.090 --> 00:11:33.059
we get back to headquarters.

00:11:33.059 --> 00:11:34.960
Aero: I keep telling
you-that's not a farmer's

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:37.196
market-it's a pet store.

00:11:37.196 --> 00:11:40.232
Amethyst: No, no no-n-not
that-I forgot my ID.

00:11:40.232 --> 00:11:42.668
We have to go
to my apartment.

00:11:42.668 --> 00:11:45.771
Aero: Y-Y-Y-YOUR
apartment-as in

00:11:45.771 --> 00:11:48.174
[with outrage]
Y-O-U-R-YOUR-apartment?

00:11:48.174 --> 00:11:49.208
Amethyst: R-Relax!

00:11:49.208 --> 00:11:50.810
It'll be fine.

00:11:50.810 --> 00:11:52.578
Aero: Look-I just
remember the holiday

00:11:52.578 --> 00:11:54.547
party a few years back!

00:11:54.547 --> 00:11:56.415
Amethyst: I took
care of the badger.

00:11:56.415 --> 00:11:58.150
You'll see,
it's no problem!

00:12:01.053 --> 00:12:03.055
Aeon: Well-this place
is a reality show

00:12:03.055 --> 00:12:04.423
waiting to happen...

00:12:04.423 --> 00:12:06.859
Amethyst: Hey-I don't
judge you for that perm.

00:12:06.859 --> 00:12:10.796
1993 called, it wants
its hairstyle back!

00:12:10.796 --> 00:12:12.798
[cutesy voice]
Hello, Sprinkles.

00:12:12.798 --> 00:12:15.201
[cutesy voice]
Hello, Mr. Giggles.

00:12:15.201 --> 00:12:18.270
[cutesy voice] Hello,
Cuddie-fluffle-wuffle.

00:12:18.270 --> 00:12:21.040
[cutesy voice] Hello,
Dr. Cutesyhugs, holder of

00:12:21.040 --> 00:12:23.742
PhD in cuddles.

00:12:23.742 --> 00:12:27.446
[cutesy voice]
Hello, Stripes the Tiger.

00:12:27.446 --> 00:12:30.349
Aeon: Ok, Stripes is
definitely a raccoon.

00:12:30.349 --> 00:12:32.518
Amethyst: Nah-you're a raccoon.

00:12:32.518 --> 00:12:34.720
Aeon: Just hurry up
and find your ID.

00:12:34.720 --> 00:12:36.388
Amethyst: Don't worry,
it's right here underneath

00:12:36.388 --> 00:12:38.390
my dinner-from Tuesday.

00:12:38.390 --> 00:12:39.925
Aeon: -It's-FRIDAY!!!

00:12:39.925 --> 00:12:42.761
Amethyst: Oh,
and-YOU'VE-never had leftovers?!

00:12:42.761 --> 00:12:45.197
Aeon: We SERIOUSLY have to
deal with the particulate matter

00:12:45.197 --> 00:12:48.501
in here-this place is
an absolute biohazard!

00:12:48.501 --> 00:12:49.301
Amethyst: What do you mean?

00:12:49.301 --> 00:12:51.137
I'm not burning
anything in here.

00:12:51.137 --> 00:12:53.239
How is there
particulate matter?

00:12:53.239 --> 00:12:55.541
Aeon: Not all particulate
matter is chemical.

00:12:55.541 --> 00:12:58.077
Aeon: A huge amount of
particulate matter comes from

00:12:58.077 --> 00:13:00.813
a biological,
or living, origin.

00:13:00.813 --> 00:13:02.715
Amethyst: Oh,
sure, like pollen?

00:13:02.715 --> 00:13:04.049
I know all about that!

00:13:04.049 --> 00:13:04.850
Aeon: [surprised] You do?

00:13:04.850 --> 00:13:07.520
Amethyst: Yea, my
allergies are crazy bad.

00:13:07.520 --> 00:13:10.356
Pollen is the male
reproductive cell in a plant.

00:13:10.356 --> 00:13:13.325
Amethyst: Many trees release
billions of pollen grains to

00:13:13.325 --> 00:13:15.761
fertilize other
trees and form seeds.

00:13:15.761 --> 00:13:17.830
Amethyst: Pollen can be
carried by insects or other

00:13:17.830 --> 00:13:20.166
pollinating animals
between plants.

00:13:20.166 --> 00:13:23.135
Amethyst: This pollen is usually
used by flowering plants, and

00:13:23.135 --> 00:13:25.871
doesn't create a lot
of problems for humans.

00:13:25.871 --> 00:13:28.274
Amethyst: Other plants use
the wind to carry pollen,

00:13:28.274 --> 00:13:30.709
THOSE plants
are the problem.

00:13:30.709 --> 00:13:32.344
Amethyst: This pollen
can aggravate symptoms of

00:13:32.344 --> 00:13:34.380
hay fever or asthma.

00:13:34.380 --> 00:13:38.384
Amethyst: This impacts about 25% of the population in the U.S.

00:13:38.384 --> 00:13:41.654
Amethyst: [sniffles]-Uh
oh...ah ah ahhhhhhchoo!

00:13:41.654 --> 00:13:43.088
Aeon: Let me help out here.

00:13:43.088 --> 00:13:45.391
Aeon: Pollen counts in the
air are highest in the early

00:13:45.391 --> 00:13:48.127
morning hours
between 5 and 10 AM.

00:13:48.127 --> 00:13:51.330
Aeon: Dry, windy, hot days are
ideal times for pollen to be

00:13:51.330 --> 00:13:54.700
released, so watch out if
you know this impacts you.

00:13:54.700 --> 00:13:55.834
Amethyst: [sniffling]
Look you see?

00:13:55.834 --> 00:13:58.404
That's why I don't have
ANY plants in here.

00:13:58.404 --> 00:14:00.773
Aeon: Ok, but you
still have some MAJOR

00:14:00.773 --> 00:14:02.675
particulate
matter sources.

00:14:02.675 --> 00:14:04.210
Aeon: Haven't you noticed
all those green and white

00:14:04.210 --> 00:14:06.645
fuzzy patches all
over your apartment?

00:14:06.645 --> 00:14:10.916
Amethyst: Oh, you mean the
snuggle patches on my walls?

00:14:10.916 --> 00:14:13.052
Aeon: [with outrage] Those
AREN'T snuggle patches!

00:14:13.052 --> 00:14:13.886
They're MOLD!

00:14:13.886 --> 00:14:14.720
FUNGUS!

00:14:14.720 --> 00:14:15.788
BAD!

00:14:15.788 --> 00:14:16.789
Amethyst: Aw come on...

00:14:16.789 --> 00:14:18.791
How can fungus
hurt anybody?

00:14:18.791 --> 00:14:20.993
The word "fun"
is right in it!

00:14:20.993 --> 00:14:23.262
Aeon: [with
disbelief] Oh gosh-ok!

00:14:23.262 --> 00:14:25.364
Similar to plants-fungi have

00:14:25.364 --> 00:14:27.733
reproductive cells
called spores.

00:14:27.733 --> 00:14:30.169
Aeon: Like pollen, fungal
spores can be carried by

00:14:30.169 --> 00:14:32.538
the wind and insects
or even in water.

00:14:32.538 --> 00:14:35.040
Aeon: In fact, fungal
spores are more common in

00:14:35.040 --> 00:14:36.842
the atmosphere than pollen.

00:14:36.842 --> 00:14:39.912
Amethyst: But can spores cause
the same problems as pollen?

00:14:39.912 --> 00:14:41.347
Aeon: They sure can.

00:14:41.347 --> 00:14:43.916
Spores can cause allergen
side-effects like

00:14:43.916 --> 00:14:46.585
sneezing, runny nose,
mucous production,

00:14:46.585 --> 00:14:50.489
Aeon: cough, congestion,
earache, headache, wheezing,

00:14:50.489 --> 00:14:53.259
asthma, or other
illnesses like asthma.

00:14:53.259 --> 00:14:54.426
Amethyst: Oh great...

00:14:54.426 --> 00:14:55.694
Aeon: I'm not done yet.

00:14:55.694 --> 00:14:58.497
Aeon: The worst bit is that
fungi release chemicals called

00:14:58.497 --> 00:15:01.033
mycotoxins when they
break down their food.

00:15:01.033 --> 00:15:03.269
Aeon: These mycotoxins
can also get on spores

00:15:03.269 --> 00:15:05.004
before they enter your body.

00:15:05.004 --> 00:15:08.140
Aeon: In your body, mycotoxins
can cause infections.

00:15:08.140 --> 00:15:11.210
Some of these mycotoxins
can cause cancer,

00:15:11.210 --> 00:15:14.113
asthma-like illnesses,
and some are even fatal.

00:15:14.113 --> 00:15:14.713
Amethyst: Ah!

00:15:14.713 --> 00:15:17.950
Ok, get rid of the mold,
get rid of the mold!

00:15:17.950 --> 00:15:19.752
Aeon: I'm not done yet.

00:15:19.752 --> 00:15:21.587
We still need to
talk about THOSE!

00:15:21.587 --> 00:15:22.554
Amethyst: AUGH!

00:15:22.554 --> 00:15:24.857
Not my preciouses!

00:15:24.857 --> 00:15:26.258
Aeon: Not just the cats.

00:15:26.258 --> 00:15:28.827
Aeon: It's also the nasty
dust all over this place.

00:15:28.827 --> 00:15:30.329
Your dirty clothes,

00:15:30.329 --> 00:15:31.997
Aeon: these sheets you
probably haven't changed

00:15:31.997 --> 00:15:33.899
since YOLO was a thing.

00:15:33.899 --> 00:15:35.200
Amethyst: What about them?

00:15:35.200 --> 00:15:37.336
Aeon: They're all
encouraging dust mites.

00:15:37.336 --> 00:15:39.738
Amethyst: Dust-mites-?

00:15:39.738 --> 00:15:41.407
Aeon: Here-look!

00:15:41.407 --> 00:15:42.741
Dust mites!

00:15:42.741 --> 00:15:45.511
Aeon: These little guys
are microscopic arachnids,

00:15:45.511 --> 00:15:47.546
the relatives of
spiders and ticks.

00:15:47.546 --> 00:15:49.214
Aeon: They feed on the
flakes of skin that

00:15:49.214 --> 00:15:52.217
people and animals
shed ALL-THE-TIME!

00:15:52.217 --> 00:15:55.087
Amethyst:
Gross-get a life, guys!

00:15:55.087 --> 00:15:57.756
Aeon: Well-we do need
them-otherwise that stuff

00:15:57.756 --> 00:16:01.627
would just sit around and
we'd be wading in dead skin-

00:16:01.627 --> 00:16:03.329
Aeon: but we don't need
to provide them with an

00:16:03.329 --> 00:16:06.332
International House of
Detritus-like you have.

00:16:06.332 --> 00:16:08.600
Aeon: The remains dust
mites leave behind are

00:16:08.600 --> 00:16:11.270
the main cause of dust
allergies in people,

00:16:11.270 --> 00:16:13.772
Aeon: And they're
found EVERYWHERE.

00:16:13.772 --> 00:16:16.675
Aeon: Mattresses, pillows,
bed linens, carpets,

00:16:16.675 --> 00:16:20.446
draperies, upholstered
furniture, even stuffed toys.

00:16:20.446 --> 00:16:23.082
Amethyst: Ok, fungal
spores and dust mites.

00:16:23.082 --> 00:16:24.783
Amethyst: This place is
literally filled with

00:16:24.783 --> 00:16:26.018
particulate matter.

00:16:26.018 --> 00:16:27.653
How can I fix it?

00:16:27.653 --> 00:16:32.157
Aeon: Well-for the mites
we need to WASH-YOUR-STUFF!

00:16:32.157 --> 00:16:34.927
Aeon: You should be washing your
sheets weekly in water above

00:16:34.927 --> 00:16:38.597
130 degrees (F°) to
take care of the mites.

00:16:38.597 --> 00:16:42.601
Aeon: Also, make sure that all
of this dust is cleaned-vacuum

00:16:42.601 --> 00:16:45.571
regularly to keep the dust
and cat hair from collecting.

00:16:45.571 --> 00:16:48.207
Aeon: For the spores, make
sure you have all the areas of

00:16:48.207 --> 00:16:50.876
your apartment well
ventilated to prevent moisture.

00:16:50.876 --> 00:16:53.178
Aeon: I would also suggest
that you maybe start wrapping

00:16:53.178 --> 00:16:57.549
your food and-like use the FRIDGE-instead of the floor-!

00:16:57.549 --> 00:17:00.986
Aeon: However, we already
have mold growing on the walls.

00:17:00.986 --> 00:17:03.389
Aeon: We need to clean up
this stuff with BLEACH-like

00:17:03.389 --> 00:17:05.691
5 or 6 of these!

00:17:05.691 --> 00:17:06.725
Aeon: Much better.

00:17:06.725 --> 00:17:07.593
[Action music playing]
Amethyst: We better get back

00:17:07.593 --> 00:17:08.961
to headquarters quick.

00:17:08.961 --> 00:17:10.829
The Commander's
going to be steamed.

00:17:15.267 --> 00:17:16.235
Amethyst: Hey, Steve.

00:17:16.235 --> 00:17:17.836
Aeon: Wait-Amethyst!

00:17:17.836 --> 00:17:18.670
-This isn't!

00:17:18.670 --> 00:17:19.238
-Hey!

00:17:19.238 --> 00:17:20.038
-Wait!

00:17:22.608 --> 00:17:24.376
Amethyst: [laughing]-So
then, we got her to

00:17:24.376 --> 00:17:25.644
stop burning the records

00:17:25.644 --> 00:17:27.913
Amethyst: because this guy
was singing songs about how

00:17:27.913 --> 00:17:31.183
being a 15 year-old-girl
was so hard!

00:17:31.183 --> 00:17:33.952
Aeon: Hey-Amethyst-don't
you notice something weird

00:17:33.952 --> 00:17:36.622
going on
here-[startled]-AAH!!

00:17:36.622 --> 00:17:38.123
Aeon: What's with
the commander?!

00:17:38.123 --> 00:17:39.691
Amethyst: [whispering]
Look-he's sensitive about that

00:17:39.691 --> 00:17:42.060
new hairpiece-be nice!

00:17:42.060 --> 00:17:44.496
Aeon: That's-NOT-a wig!

00:17:44.496 --> 00:17:46.432
Amethyst: Ok, now you're
just trying to oversell it.

00:17:46.432 --> 00:17:47.366
Aeon: No-look!

00:17:47.366 --> 00:17:50.502
-It's-uh-It's a MUSHROOM!

00:17:50.502 --> 00:17:52.671
Amethyst: [gasp!] You're right!

00:17:52.671 --> 00:17:53.739
-[with surprise]-
Oh my gosh!

00:17:53.739 --> 00:17:57.209
Amethyst: This green
haze must be spores!

00:17:57.209 --> 00:17:58.844
They're everywhere!

00:17:58.844 --> 00:18:00.946
Aeon: Ok-what are
we going to do?

00:18:00.946 --> 00:18:01.947
Amethyst: Looks
like the spores are

00:18:01.947 --> 00:18:03.282
coming out of the vents.

00:18:03.282 --> 00:18:04.883
Amethyst: I'll go look for
the source, you take care of

00:18:04.883 --> 00:18:06.251
the commander's office.

00:18:06.251 --> 00:18:07.352
[Suspense-Action music]
Aeon: Deal.

00:18:09.521 --> 00:18:12.524
Aeon: Woah-these must
be military grade.

00:18:12.524 --> 00:18:14.760
Amethyst: [suspense-action
music]-[grunting] Almost there.

00:18:14.760 --> 00:18:21.800
[Gasping for air]-
Must-keep-going.

00:18:21.800 --> 00:18:24.937
[Gasping for air]-
Must-keep-going.

00:18:24.937 --> 00:18:25.904
[action music]
Aeon: Let' do this.

00:18:28.140 --> 00:18:29.908
Fun Guy: Ignore me will he?

00:18:29.908 --> 00:18:31.910
-Scoff at my ideas?

00:18:31.910 --> 00:18:35.180
Fun Guy: [Giggling] Well,
frankly, Commander Cadmium,

00:18:35.180 --> 00:18:37.616
I find you to be
a-[brief pause]-

00:18:37.616 --> 00:18:43.989
SPORE-[evil laughter]-muah hahahahahahahaha!!!!!

00:18:43.989 --> 00:18:45.958
Amethyst: How do I get out of this vent?

00:18:45.958 --> 00:18:51.196
-whoa-whoa-whoaaah! -
heh-hah! -Smooth...

00:18:51.196 --> 00:18:53.599
Amethyst: The gig's
up Fun Guy Fern...OHH!

00:18:53.599 --> 00:18:58.537
-Ohh-FUN-GUY-FERN-ohh-like
fungi!

00:18:58.537 --> 00:19:00.706
Amethyst: Oh my gosh, that
makes so much sense now.

00:19:00.706 --> 00:19:04.376
F: It's too late Amethyst,
I've already taken over!

00:19:04.376 --> 00:19:07.079
[secret agent music]

00:19:07.079 --> 00:19:08.247
Aero: You were saying?

00:19:10.015 --> 00:19:12.518
Cadmium: For protecting
the Super Hidden Humans from

00:19:12.518 --> 00:19:15.888
the dangers of particulate
matter-both chemical AND

00:19:15.888 --> 00:19:20.058
organic-I promote you
two to level 8 agents.

00:19:20.058 --> 00:19:23.529
Cadmium: [whispers] Now you
get to know-Phil's still alive.

00:19:23.529 --> 00:19:26.164
Hairy Agent: Graaaaaar!

00:19:26.164 --> 00:19:28.800
[Action music playing]

